 "title": "core", "category": "Framework", "author": "irpina",
 "description": "The boot copier and the hook bus for the Octatrack: it reserves the bottom of the sample and recorder memory for mods, only the 6 KB pages their RAM fills (0.2 took 10 MB), copies their code there at boot and checks the copy against the linker's hash (it halts on a mismatch rather than run it), and calls them on the UI tick, the screen, the keys, the encoders, MIDI in and out, the audio frame, its start and its end, the transport, the end of boot, the idle loop and a 120 Hz tick. It times every audio frame, writes page-2 knobs the way the panel does, and paces MIDI out. From 0.6 it tells mods when a project is loaded, made, saved and reloaded, runs their card work on the engine task, keeps their data with the project and on the card in files the stock OS ignores, and gives them battery RAM. From 0.7 it tells mods when a voice starts, releases, binds to its sample, ends and has its locks applied, and when the DSP's record and trig flags for a track are written, and lets them change or take the ones that can be. From 0.8 it tells mods of the edits their data must follow (a pattern or a track through the clipboard and the undo buffer, where a paste or an undo may be refused; a Part saved, reloaded, changed or set to its defaults; the start of a project load), of a voice about to be reset (it may be kept), of the boot before the OS, and lets them change the track icons and the SETUP windows' knobs. Every linkable Octatrack mod needs it. On its own it changes nothing else the unit does.",
 "device": "octatrack", "os": "1.40C",
 "sources": ["core-ot.s", "bus.s", "exports.c", "store.s", "store.c", "voice.s",
  "edit.s", "edit.c", "screen.s", "screen.c"],
